{"seq":26,"slug":"financial-risk-management","title":"金融风险管理","stage":"DONE","category":"economics-finance","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"金融风险管理\">金融风险管理</h1><p>金融的本质是在不确定中配置资本，而风险管理就是把这种不确定性变得可测量、可定价、可控制的工程。一笔贷款会不会违约、一个交易组合明天可能亏多少、一家银行能否在挤兑中存活、整个金融系统会不会在某次冲击下连锁崩塌——这些问题表面上各不相同，背后却共享同一套思维：先用统计语言刻画损失的分布，再用资本、对冲与限额去约束尾部，最后用监管与压力测试检验这套约束在极端情况下是否真的成立。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 沿着「如何量化与控制金融风险」这条主线展开，分四章逐级递进。</p>\n<p>第一章「风险管理基础」搭建整个 hub 的度量地基。它先厘清市场、信用、流动性、操作等风险类型的边界，再补齐刻画损失分布所需的统计工具——波动率、相关性、肥尾与极值，最后落到两个贯穿全 hub 的核心度量：风险价值 VaR 与预期损失 ES。后面每一章谈到「损失有多大」时，用的都是这一章定义的语言。</p>\n<p>第二章「市场风险与信用风险」把度量工具用到金融机构面对的两类主要风险上。市场风险关心价格波动，对应的是希腊字母与对冲；信用风险关心交易对手违约，对应的是违约概率 PD、违约损失率 LGD 与违约敞口 EAD 这套分解。流动性风险与操作风险作为第三类，提醒我们：让机构倒下的往往不是估值损失，而是融不到钱或一次操作失灵。</p>\n<p>第三章「监管与压力测试」把视角从单笔头寸抬升到整家机构乃至整个系统。巴塞尔协议规定了银行必须为风险持有多少资本，压力测试检验机构在假想的极端情景下是否还活得下去，系统性风险则追问：当所有机构都按同样的规则去对冲时，这种一致行动本身会不会制造出新的、更大的风险。这一章完成从微观审慎到宏观审慎的跨越。</p>\n<p>第四章「前沿」转向 2025–2026 年正在重塑风险版图的三股力量：气候与 ESG 风险把损失的时间尺度拉长到几十年，AI 与机器学习既是新的风险来源也是新的管理工具，加密资产与网络攻击则带来了传统框架尚未完全消化的新型风险。它们的共同点是：旧的度量与监管框架正在被迫扩展和重写。</p>\n<p>四章之间是地基、应用、约束、延伸的关系。建议初学者按顺序通读；有特定问题的读者可以从对应章节切入，每篇文档都会在引用其它篇主讲的概念时给出交叉链接，让你随时回到它的源头。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"风险管理基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-core-concepts","title":"金融风险管理导论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/foundations/intro-and-core-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"risk-measurement-statistics","title":"风险度量的统计基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/foundations/risk-measurement-statistics"},{"seq":3,"slug":"var-expected-shortfall","title":"VaR与预期损失","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/foundations/var-expected-shortfall"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"market-credit-risk","title":"市场风险与信用风险","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/market-credit-risk","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"market-risk-hedging","title":"市场风险与对冲","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/market-credit-risk/market-risk-hedging"},{"seq":2,"slug":"credit-risk","title":"信用风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/market-credit-risk/credit-risk"},{"seq":3,"slug":"liquidity-operational-risk","title":"流动性与操作风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/market-credit-risk/liquidity-operational-risk"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"regulation-stress-testing","title":"监管与压力测试","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/regulation-stress-testing","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"basel-capital-regulation","title":"巴塞尔协议与资本监管","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/regulation-stress-testing/basel-capital-regulation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"stress-testing-scenarios","title":"压力测试与情景分析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/regulation-stress-testing/stress-testing-scenarios"},{"seq":3,"slug":"systemic-risk","title":"系统性风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/regulation-stress-testing/systemic-risk"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"frontiers","title":"前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"climate-esg-risk","title":"气候与ESG风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/frontiers/climate-esg-risk"},{"seq":2,"slug":"ai-ml-risk-management","title":"AI与机器学习风险管理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/frontiers/ai-ml-risk-management"},{"seq":3,"slug":"crypto-cyber-emerging-risk","title":"加密与新型风险","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/financial-risk-management/frontiers/crypto-cyber-emerging-risk"}]}]}